From 79f9cbab0544aed15258e944ba6d53e8c5e6362b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Sumner <mdsumner@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 01:17:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] merge_rasters: mosaic via VRT, warp once

Replace the two-pass warp (mosaic to GeoTIFF, then reproject) with
gdalbuildvrt over the tile files followed by a single warp.

Warping the tiles as separate sources introduced NA and resampling
artifacts along tile seams because each source is warped independently
and the resampling kernel is truncated at tile edges; the two-pass
approach worked around this at the cost of writing and re-reading the
full-resolution mosaic. A VRT is a small XML index with no pixel I/O,
and gives the warper one contiguous dataset, so the seam problem is
fixed exactly with one warp pass.

Verified against an analytic surface on synthetic tiles: naive
multi-source warp max seam error 0.014 m; two-pass and VRT both exact
(0 m) against a reference warp of a pre-merged raster, and the VRT
output is pixel-identical to the two-pass output. Adds offline tests
covering the seam case, single-file input, returnRaster = FALSE, and
target_prj = NULL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
